<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Morkels half yr shr dips, no div.</title>
<headline>Morkels half yr shr dips, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30 1996 (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     15.6	  vs   17.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  -	    vs    -</p>
<p>    Retained income	 10.59	 vs   8.42</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   17.38	 vs  12.99</p>
<p>    Tax			  6.79	 vs   4.57</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    8.90	 vs   6.49</p>
<p>    Turnover		 394.75	 vs 268.49</p>
<p>Full name:  Morkels Retail Group Ltd (industrial-stores)</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said prospects for the year to March 1997 remained positive but the three peak trading months through to January would be critical in the light of softer demand already experienced in the retail sector.</p>
<p>Given reasonable trading conditions, management believed the group was well positioned to achieve its budget objectives for the year to March.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
